From 1d1bcef21f824f357feff3a3df980472567a71db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "5455945@gmail.com" <5455945@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:03:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] tools: complete the sync opt-in flow and add website SSO

Sync opt-in:
  * /enable_sync now returns action=ENABLE_SYNC and is driven automatically
    after sign-in (1.5s auto-navigation; --no-auto-enable-sync makes it a
    button-only step).
  * Opening /signin/chrome/sync with an existing session shows the
    "Turn on sync" step instead of the password form.
  * This fixes the "refresh token present but Not Signed In" state that
    Chromium reaches when the DICE ENABLE_SYNC header is never emitted
    (chrome/browser/signin/dice_response_handler.cc).

Website SSO:
  * /portal: demo "official website" that reflects the browser session.
  * /authorize: OAuth2 authorization-code endpoint so a site on any origin
    can reuse the browser login; redirect_uri is validated against
    --oauth-redirect-uris (default: same origin only).
  * --cookie-domain / --cookie-samesite for sibling-subdomain SSO.
  * --cors-origins for credentialed /api/session and userinfo calls.

Tests: 34 total (portal, authorize, CORS, cookie attributes added).
